```
This assert statement checks that the count of the list increases by one after an item is added. The `OLD(Count)` part retrieves the old value of the count before the operation, and `RET` refers to the return value of the function, which is the new count after the operation. The assert statement is true if and only if the list's count increases by one after an item is added.
