```cs
public virtual int Count
{
    get
    {
        //NotpAssume.IsTrue(index >= 0 && index < _size);
        if (index < 0 || index >= _size) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException("nameof(index)", "SR.ArgumentOutOfRange_Index");


        return _size;
    }
}
```
In the above code, the 'RET' variable refers to the return value of the method 'Count'. The 'OLD(RET)' indicates the old value of the return value of the function at the beginning of the function. Therefore, the assert statement checks if the new value (RET) of the function is greater than or equal to the old value. This is the expected behavior because the number of elements in the list (RET) should not decrease.
